>> title: Makhani Gravy
>> category: Sauces & Gravies
>> tags: indian, tomato, cashew, butter, base
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: makhani sauce, butter gravy, makhani base, tomato cashew gravy
>> pairs-with: butter-chicken, ginger-garlic-paste
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr
>> step.1: simmer 25 min, until the cashews go soft
>> step.2: blend smooth, push through the sieve
>> step.3: simmer 10 min, until it holds a line
>> step.4: whisk in off the heat

Simmer @canned whole tomatoes{28%oz}(800 g), @raw cashews{1/2%cup}(70 g), @ginger-garlic paste{1%Tbs}(17 g), @green chiles{2}(slit), @green cardamom{4%pods}(bruised), @cinnamon{1%stick}(2-in piece), @water{1%cup}(240 mL) and @kosher salt{2%tsp} in a #heavy pot{} ~simmer{25%min}.

Blend @&(~1)tomato and cashew{} in a #blender{} until it is completely smooth, then push it through a #fine sieve{} with a ladle. The sieve is not optional — the cardamom husk and the tomato skin are what stand between this and the velvet it is supposed to be.

Simmer @&(~1)strained gravy{} with @butter{4%Tbs}(56 g), @Kashmiri chile powder{1%Tbs} and @honey{1%Tbs}(21 g) ~simmer{10%min}, until a spoon drawn across the bottom holds its line for a second.

Whisk @heavy cream{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @kasuri methi{1%Tbs}(crumbled between the palms) and @cold butter{3%Tbs}(42 g; cubed) into @&(~1)gravy{} off the heat ~whisk{2%min}, adding the cold butter a cube at a time so it thickens the sauce instead of splitting out of it.

This gravy and the one under chicken tikka masala are the same tomato and the same cashews; the difference is how much butter goes in cold at the end and whether the chicken was charred first. Six cups, which is butter chicken for six or two dinners for three.
